course: dictionary
lesson: 5479
title: Many meanings of last
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word last has several meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one. Read the clues: «The last piece is for you.» Here last means the one at the end, after all the others.
explain: Look at «The last known one died in a zoo in 1936.» Known and 1936 tell you that last means the most recent one before now. In «last week», last means the one just before this week. Always ask: what does the rest of the sentence say about time or order?
explain: Last can also be a verb, which means to go on for a time. «The chip has no battery, lasts for life» tells you it keeps working for a whole life. Swap in another word, like keeps going, and check it still makes sense.
fact: Last can be an adjective, an adverb, a verb or a noun.
fact: «Last» can mean coming at the end, or the one just before this one, as in «last year».
fact: «At last» means finally, after a long wait.
fact: «To last» means to go on for a time, or to stay good or useful.
fact: «Last but not least» introduces the final one with respect.
exercise: «A vulture lands last, bald and scruffy.» What does last mean here? | Finally, after a long wait | To go on for a time | *At the end, after all the others | The one just before this one
exercise: «Most microchips carry a number; the chip has no battery and lasts for life.» What does lasts mean? | Hides from view | Is the one before this one | Lands at the end | *Keeps working for a long time
exercise: «J, U and W were added to English only in the last thousand years.» What does last mean? | Going on for a time | *The most recent thousand years, the ones just before now | The very end of a thousand years | Finally, after a long wait
test: «At last the bus arrived, after an hour of waiting.» What does at last mean? | At the very end of the bus route | *Finally, after a long wait | Going on for a time | Last week
test: In «last year», what does last mean? | Coming at the end | Finally | *The one just before this one | To go on for a time
exam: «The thylacine was the last known one of its kind, and no proof of any living since has been found.» Which meaning of last fits, and why? | The worst one, as in came dead last | The very end of a line, because it means final | To go on for a long time, because a thylacine lasts | *The most recent one, because known and since show it is about time before now
